    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d456">

                <pb facs="0416" n="409" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg409"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/9353: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-08-14T18:00:00+08:00">August 14, 1937—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 14—8:38 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>481. Increasingly heavy bombing by Chinese air craft at Shanghai is going on.
                    Their objective is Japanese flagship tied up near Japanese Consulate General.
                    There are urgent pleas that this war vessel proceed to an anchorage down stream
                    as its present situation is bringing bombs short dropped into the area of
                    foreign refuge where a large number have been killed and others, including
                    Americans, wounded. Situation grave. I have asked Embassy, Nanking, to make
                        representations.<anchor n="7" xml:id="d456-f1"/></p>
                <p>Repeated to Department and Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
